robe -v error -show_entries format=duration -of default=noprint_wrappers=1:nokey=1 '$nc'\" 2>/dev/null | tail -1)\n\n=== the ffprobe call on segments ===\n46-#   \"probe OK while flag set\" fired a standing FALSE RECOVERY on\n47-#   every run (live: 18:04 -03 feeder run, newest segment duration\n48:#   412523s). Fix: pair the tail decode with an ffprobe duration\n49-#   check (sane = 16.0s, threshold 60s). RECOVERY now requires BOTH\n50-#   decode AND sane duration. Poisoned + flag = watch state (quiet);\n51-#   poisoned + flag withdrawn = NEW sighting, fails loudly. The\n52-#   KNOWN_FAULT contract is otherwise unchanged. Verified live on\n53-#   sophon (canonical runner): poisoned newest segment (515652s) ->\n--\n437-  # ext1 segments are 16.0s; poisoned are >=28h (or transient stubs\n438-  # <6s, which already fail the tail decode). Threshold 60s.\n439:  segdur=$($P exec frigate sh -c \"/usr/lib/ffmpeg/7.0/bin/ffprobe -v error -show_entries format=duration -of default=noprint_wrappers=1:nokey=1 '$nc'\" 2>/dev/null | tail -1)\n440-  segpoisoned=0\n441-  case \"$segdur\" in\n442-    \"\"|*[!0-9.]*) segpoisoned=0 ;;  # unparsable: do not double-alarm, the decode result stands\n443-    *) awk -v d=\"$segdur\" 'BEGIN{exit !(d>60)}' && segpoisoned=1 ;;\n444-  esac\n\n[t+07:41/60:00 c57/300]"},{"role":"assistant","content":null,"tool_calls":[{"id":"call_3kenpbwn","function":{"index":0,"name":"execute_code_local","arguments":{"command":"timeout 20 ssh -i /root/.ssh/id_ed25519 -o UserKnownHostsFile=/tmp/aria_known_hosts root@10.66.0.5 'echo \"=== fleet-check.sh: where does it find the segment files (line 340-380) ===\"; sed -n \"340,380p\" /var/home/nacho/repos/iar-personalization/knowledge/aria/bin/fleet-check.sh' 2>&1"}}}]},{"role":"tool","content":"[04:02:24] === fleet-check.sh: where does it find the segment files (line 340-380) ===\n# watch state; segments fresh again = RECOVERY, FAIL loudly (withdraw\n# by emptying KNOWN_FAULT_EXT2_SEG after verification).\nKNOWN_FA